&= \frac{1}{F_1 F_3} + \frac{F_3}{F_2 (F_3 + F_2)} + \frac{F_4}{F_3 (F_4 + F_3)} + \dotsb
\end{align*}

Now, we can simplify the terms:

\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{F_{n + 1}}{F_n F_{n + 2}} &= \frac{1}{F_1 F_3} + \frac{F_3}{F_2 (F_3 + F_2)} + \frac{F_4}{F_3 (F_4 + F_3)} + \dotsb \\
